summary:
  "Show more" stops when the next page's planned thirty rows would reach the
  300, whatever the page before it really brought.

history:
  The button and the request held the 300-row ceiling against the cap
  planned for the page. With 270 rows up the cap went to 300, the page gave
  49 duplicates and one new station, and at 271 rows the button was gone and
  a click asked nothing, the directory still holding more. The ceiling is
  held against the rows on screen.

target:
  package/contents/ui/SearchLogic.js

find:
      return !!page && page.more === true && typeof shown === "number" && shown < ceiling;

replace:
      return !!page && page.more === true && typeof shown === "number" && shown + 30 <= ceiling;

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_searchlogic.qml::test_the_ceiling_is_held_against_the_rows_on_screen.
  Line-neutral.
